{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — Some say: the King is joined with הושיעה [save], but this is not correct because of the etnaḥ. And others said: it is inverted — 'in the day we call, YHWH, save' — as is the practice of those who wage war when they return." "<b>יעננו</b> [He will answer us] — The King, who is David, said: Amen, may it be so. And this is in the manner of 'Blessed is he who comes,' as I shall explain. But the correct interpretation is: 'He will save us,' for HaShem knows his thought, and thus 'אנה YHWH הושיעה נא' [please, YHWH, save now]. The verb is not written, and the King is HaShem, for He is the King in truth, for David is His anointed."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:02.260417011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}